{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq 'keys' task/resources/final/manifest.json; rg -n 'def .*bootstrap|def .*aggregate|def .*metric|gain_ci|baseline_mae|candidate_diagnostics_trust|np.quantile' task/evaluate_final.py | tail -35; sed -n '1,115p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_local_residual_medians/program_1/src/RESIDUAL_METHOD.md\"","aggregated_output":"[\n  \"allocation\",\n  \"columns\",\n  \"coverage_rule\",\n  \"cross_plane_disjoint\",\n  \"exclusions\",\n  \"license_evidence\",\n  \"limitations\",\n  \"normalization\",\n  \"peer_aliases\",\n  \"peer_document_hashes\",\n  \"peer_families\",\n  \"peer_row_hashes\",\n  \"peer_source_ids\",\n  \"repository\",\n  \"revision\",\n  \"schema_version\",\n  \"source_row_count\"\n]\n34:METRIC_NAMES = ['combined_score', 'mae', 'rmse', 'baseline_mae', 'delta_best_baseline', 'constant_control_mae', 'permuted_control_mae', 'reset_max_abs_delta', 'correct', 'mae_k1', 'mae_k2', 'mae_k4', 'mae_k8', 'gain_ci_low', 'gain_ci_high']\n976:def aggregate(episodes, outcomes, complete):\n980:    baseline_maes = [fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['baselines'][method].mean()) for index in primary]) for method in range(5)]\n981:    baseline_mae = min(baseline_maes)\n988:               'baseline_mae': baseline_mae, 'delta_best_baseline': baseline_mae-mae if complete else -1.0,\n995:        metrics['gain_ci_low'], metrics['gain_ci_high'] = -1.0, -1.0\n999:def bootstrap_gain(episodes, outcomes, rows):\n1016:    intervals = np.quantile(samples, [.005, .995], axis=0)\n1031:                'baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint': outcome['baselines'].tolist(),\n1048:def write_outputs(directory, metrics, correct, feasible, evidence=None):\n1078:    metrics = {name: (-1.0 if name in ['delta_best_baseline', 'gain_ci_low', 'gain_ci_high'] else 1.0) for name in METRIC_NAMES}\n1112:                metrics['gain_ci_low'], metrics['gain_ci_high'] = bootstrap_gain(episodes, outcomes, rows)\n# Cross-fitted local residual medians\n\n## Scope and interface\n\n`program.py:handle` remains the only public entrypoint. No operation, response\nkey, score unit, bound, or budget is added. The full-history ALS fit and its\nrandom-number stream are unchanged. The covariance-gain selection code is\nunchanged. Only predictions on unqueried columns may receive corrections;\nqueried-column predictions retain the incumbent's behavior. A zero blend returns\nthe incumbent prediction exactly. Reset clears all fitted and trajectory state;\nbegin clears the current observations. Caches contain historical quantities,\nnever new-model scores.\n\n## Historical calibration\n\nAll calibration is inside `fit`, before any new-model observation. An independent\nseeded RNG samples at most 512 historical rows, with a column-dependent cap\ntargeting roughly 196608 cells (and a 64-row floor). Up to 16 rows having at least\nthree observed scores are allocated to two validation folds. Each validation\nfold is excluded from both its fitted predictor and every donor fit/pool.\n\nWithin each outer training pool, up to 128 historical donors are split into two\nfolds. Each donor fold is predicted by an ALS fit on the pool minus that entire\nfold. Non-donor training rows may be used by both fits. Auxiliary fits use the\nsame ALS/ridge estimator but at most 12 sweeps; this resource approximation does\nnot change the incumbent fit. Small histories without enough validation support\nreturn the unchanged incumbent.\n\nFor a queried column set, each donor's own available anchor scores condition its\ncross-fitted predictor. A residual is its actual observed target score minus\nthat clipped conditional prediction. Missing target cells remain missing;\nneither imputed targets nor the new model's predicted scores are donor labels.\nResidual matrices are cached for up to eight queried sets per bank.\n\nDistances are mean squared standardized differences on shared observed anchors.\nScales come only from each donor model's fitting rows, with a fixed 0.025 floor\nin normalized score units. Gaussian-kernel weights are multiplied by the shared\nanchor fraction; zero-overlap donors receive zero weight. Per target, only\nfinite observed residuals with positive weights enter the weighted median.\nEffective count is squared total weight divided by squared-weight sum, using a\n1e-12 numerical floor. The correction is median times\n`blend * effective_count / (effective_count + shrinkage)`. Negligible total\nweight leaves the base prediction unchanged. Final bounds remain [0, 1].\n\n## Predeclared selection and comparisons\n\nThe grid is bandwidth `(0.35, 0.75, 1.5)`, shrinkage `(4, 16)`, and blend\n`(0, 0.25, 0.5, 1)`. The incumbent selection policy is replayed on each held-out\nhistorical row, with only its revealed scores available to prediction. Only\nhistorically observed cells can be replayed as queries. Loss is pooled absolute\nerror on finite, unqueried targets at budgets 1, 2, 4, 8 where available; rows\nwith fewer observed cells cannot contribute every budget. All configurations\nshare fits, donor pools, query trajectories, and scored cells. Zero blend wins\nties, including differences within 1e-12. The chosen local configuration is then\nused with a freshly cross-fitted donor bank from the entire sampled history.\n\nPrivate diagnostic arrays also compare the unchanged base, unconditional\nresidual medians across the shrinkage/blend grid, and direct kernel-weighted\nhistorical score medians across bandwidths. They record correction coverage and\neffective counts on the same targets. These are training diagnostics, not an\nunbiased outer evaluation, and are never included in RPC responses.\n\n## Cost, limitations, and run status\n\nThere are at most eight auxiliary ALS fits beyond the unchanged full-history\nfit: two outer predictors, four inner donor fits, and two final donor fits.\nFinal donor fits are skipped when zero blend wins. A bank has at most 128 rows;\nconditional donor prediction is batched by anchor-observation pattern. Per-target\nweighted medians sort the usable donors. All operations use NumPy on CPU.\n\nApproximate auxiliary fits and history subsampling can mismatch the incumbent.\nSparse overlap, few held-out targets, nonrepresentative donors, extrapolation,\nand multiple-configuration selection can all hurt transfer. No improvement or\nconditional-median optimality for this residual-transfer estimator is guaranteed.\nOnly supplied history, opaque column indices, and actually revealed scores are\nused; no identities, target masks, families, or evaluator metadata are assumed.\n\nThis implementation stage permits filesystem editing and static inspection only.\nNo candidate execution, tests, experiments, evaluation, literature search, or\npaper compilation has been performed. No numerical research findings are\nreported. Outer uncertainty estimates, budget/missingness experiments, crossover\nablations, a conference-format paper, and full scientific reproduction artifacts\nremain incomplete; they are not fabricated or represented as completed work.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '940,1048p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '1080,1135p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq '{repository,revision,source_row_count,n_columns:(.columns|length),normalization,coverage_rule,limitations,allocation:(.allocation|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else type end)}' task/resources/final/manifest.json; jq 'keys' task/resources/final/plan.json; rg -n 'class Baseline|def baseline|copy_skill|variance_low_rank|linear_ridge|audit|target|family' task/evaluate_final.py | head -70; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[0].solution.cases.A|{mae_dimensions:[(.mae_by_row_checkpoint|length),(.mae_by_row_checkpoint[0]|length)],baseline_dimensions:[(.baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint|length),(.baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint[0]|length)],selection_first:.selected_indices[0]}' paper_data.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '940,1048p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '1080,1135p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq '{repository,revision,source_row_count,n_columns:(.columns|length),normalization,coverage_rule,limitations,allocation:(.allocation|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else type end)}' task/resources/final/manifest.json; jq 'keys' task/resources/final/plan.json; rg -n 'class Baseline|def baseline|copy_skill|variance_low_rank|linear_ridge|audit|target|family' task/evaluate_final.py | head -70; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[0].solution.cases.A|{mae_dimensions:[(.mae_by_row_checkpoint|length),(.mae_by_row_checkpoint[0]|length)],baseline_dimensions:[(.baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint|length),(.baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint[0]|length)],selection_first:.selected_indices[0]}' paper_data.json\"","aggregated_output":"    outputs, selections = [], []\n    with until(method_deadline):\n        upload(call, values, mask)\n        ack(call({'op': 'fit', 'rank': 4, 'sweeps': sweeps, 'ridge': .1}), 'fit')\n        for trajectory, (reservoir, targets) in enumerate(partition):\n            ack(call({'op': 'begin', 'trajectory': trajectory, 'queryable': reservoir, 'budget': 8}), 'begin')\n            observed = []\n            checkpoints = []\n            for step in range(1, 9):\n                response = call({'op': 'select'})\n                if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {'index'} or type(response['index']) is not int:\n                    raise ProtocolFailure('malformed_response', 'select')\n                index = response['index']\n                if index not in reservoir or index in observed:\n                    raise ProtocolFailure('illegal_query', 'select')\n                observed.append(index)\n                ack(call({'op': 'observe', 'index': index, 'value': float(tests[trajectory, index])}), 'observe')\n                if step in CHECKPOINTS:\n                    predicted = prediction(call({'op': 'predict'}), tests.shape[1])\n                    checkpoint = CHECKPOINTS.index(step)\n                    result['mae'][trajectory, checkpoint], result['mse'][trajectory, checkpoint] = error_pair(predicted, tests[trajectory], targets)\n                    unqueried = sorted(set(np.flatnonzero(test_mask[trajectory]).tolist()) - set(observed))\n                    result['all_unqueried_mae'][trajectory, checkpoint] = error_pair(predicted, tests[trajectory], unqueried)[0]\n                    checkpoints.append(predicted.tolist())\n            outputs.append(checkpoints)\n            selections.append(observed)\n    result.update(predictions=outputs, queries=selections, duration=time.monotonic()-started, complete=True)\n    return result\n\n\ndef fixed_average(values):\n    if not values or any(not math.isfinite(value) for value in values):\n        raise ValueError('nonfinite fixed contribution')\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n\n\ndef aggregate(episodes, outcomes, complete):\n    primary = [index for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['case'] in ['A', 'B'] and not episode['replay']]\n    mae = fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mae'].mean()) for index in primary])\n    mse = fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mse'].mean()) for index in primary])\n    baseline_maes = [fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['baselines'][method].mean()) for index in primary]) for method in range(5)]\n    baseline_mae = min(baseline_maes)\n    original, replay = outcomes[0], outcomes[-1]\n    delta = 1.0\n    if original['complete'] and replay['complete'] and original['queries'] == replay['queries']:\n        delta = float(np.max(np.abs(np.asarray(original['predictions']) - np.asarray(replay['predictions']))))\n    correct = bool(complete and all(outcome['complete'] for outcome in outcomes) and delta <= 1e-10)\n    metrics = {'combined_score': 1-mae, 'mae': mae, 'rmse': math.sqrt(mse),\n               'baseline_mae': baseline_mae, 'delta_best_baseline': baseline_mae-mae if complete else -1.0,\n               'constant_control_mae': fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mae'].mean()) for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['case']=='C']),\n               'permuted_control_mae': fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mae'].mean()) for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['case']=='D']),\n               'reset_max_abs_delta': delta, 'correct': int(correct)}\n    if PLANE == 'final':\n        for checkpoint, budget in enumerate(CHECKPOINTS):\n            metrics['mae_k'+str(budget)] = fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mae'][:, checkpoint].mean()) for index in primary])\n        metrics['gain_ci_low'], metrics['gain_ci_high'] = -1.0, -1.0\n    return metrics, correct\n\n\ndef bootstrap_gain(episodes, outcomes, rows):\n    primary = [index for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['case'] in ['A', 'B'] and not episode['replay']]\n    groups = sorted({rows[row]['component'] for index in primary for row in episodes[index]['test']})\n    if not groups:\n        return -1.0, -1.0\n    group_index = {group: index for index, group in enumerate(groups)}\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(424242)\n    samples = np.zeros((400, 5))\n    for resample in range(400):\n        multiplicity = np.bincount(rng.integers(len(groups), size=len(groups)), minlength=len(groups))\n        for index in primary:\n            weights = np.asarray([multiplicity[group_index[rows[row]['component']]] for row in episodes[index]['test']], dtype=float)\n            if weights.sum() == 0:\n                samples[resample] += -np.ones(5) / len(primary)\n            else:\n                gain = outcomes[index]['baselines'].mean(axis=2) - outcomes[index]['mae'].mean(axis=1)\n                samples[resample] += gain @ weights / weights.sum() / len(primary)\n    intervals = np.quantile(samples, [.005, .995], axis=0)\n    return float(intervals[0].min()), float(intervals[1].min())\n\n\ndef make_evaluation_evidence(episodes, outcomes, rows, seeds):\n    records = []\n    for seed in seeds:\n        indices = [index for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['seed']==seed and not episode['replay']]\n        scored = [index for index in indices if episodes[index]['case'] in ['A', 'B']]\n        solution = {'cases': {}}\n        for index in indices:\n            outcome, episode = outcomes[index], episodes[index]\n            solution['cases'][episode['case']] = {\n                'completed': outcome['complete'], 'mae_by_row_checkpoint': outcome['mae'].tolist(),\n                'all_unqueried_mae_by_row_checkpoint': outcome['all_unqueried_mae'].tolist(),\n                'baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint': outcome['baselines'].tolist(),\n                'selected_indices': outcome['queries'],\n                'observed_counts': [sum(value is not None for value in rows[row]['values']) for row in episode['test']],\n                'resampling_components': [rows[row]['component'] for row in episode['test']]}\n        seed_correct = all(outcomes[index]['complete'] for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['seed']==seed)\n        if seed == episodes[0]['seed']:\n            original, replay = outcomes[0], outcomes[-1]\n            seed_correct = bool(seed_correct and original['queries'] == replay['queries']\n                                and original['predictions'] is not None and replay['predictions'] is not None\n                                and np.max(np.abs(np.asarray(original['predictions'])-np.asarray(replay['predictions']))) <= 1e-10)\n        records.append({'seed': seed, 'score': 1-fixed_average([float(outcomes[index]['mae'].mean()) for index in scored]),\n                        'correct': seed_correct,\n                        'duration_seconds': sum(outcomes[index]['duration'] for index, episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['seed']==seed),\n                        'solution': solution})\n    return {'schema_version': 1, 'episodes': records}\n\n\ndef write_outputs(directory, metrics, correct, feasible, evidence=None):\n    client = None\n    try:\n        with until(hard_deadline-finish):\n            manifest, rows, plan = load_resources()\n            preflight_wire(len(manifest['columns']))\n        episodes = [dict(episode) for episode in plan['episodes'] if not smoke or episode['seed']==SEEDS[0]]\n        if smoke:\n            for episode in episodes:\n                episode['history'] = episode['history'][:24]\n                episode['test'] = episode['test'][:4]\n        work = 1.5 if smoke else (20.0 if PLANE=='search' else 60.0)\n        profiles = {\n            'search': {'episode_count': 5 if smoke else 9, 'method_count': 6, 'wall_seconds': 120 if smoke else 1800,\n                       'startup_seconds': 5 if smoke else 120, 'finish_seconds': 5 if smoke else 30,\n                       'reset_seconds': 6, 'cleanup_seconds': 1.1, 'work_seconds': 1.5 if smoke else 20},\n            'final': {'episode_count': 5 if smoke else 13, 'method_count': 6, 'wall_seconds': 120 if smoke else 7200,\n                      'startup_seconds': 5 if smoke else 300, 'finish_seconds': 5 if smoke else 30,\n                      'reset_seconds': 6, 'cleanup_seconds': 1.1, 'work_seconds': 1.5 if smoke else 60}}\n        require_joint_workload_budget(**profiles)\n        client = CandidateClient(arguments.program_path, wall)\n        outcomes, complete = run_declared_episodes(\n            episodes, hard_deadline=hard_deadline, finish_reserve=finish, reset_timeout=6,\n            episode_overhead=5, rpc_cap=work, clock=time.monotonic, rpc=client.call,\n            evaluate=lambda episode, call, deadline: evaluate_episode(episode, call, deadline, rows=rows, smoke=smoke),\n            worst_case=worst_case,\n            record_failure=lambda failure: record_failure(dict(failure, **{\n                key: client.diagnostics[-1].get(key) if client.diagnostics else None\n                for key in ['observed_bytes', 'truncated', 'capture_error']})),\n            cleanup=client.shutdown)\n        metrics, correct = aggregate(episodes, outcomes, complete)\n        if PLANE == 'final' and complete:\n            with until(hard_deadline-5):\n                metrics['gain_ci_low'], metrics['gain_ci_high'] = bootstrap_gain(episodes, outcomes, rows)\n        evidence = make_evaluation_evidence(episodes, outcomes, rows, SEEDS[:1] if smoke else SEEDS)\n        feasible = complete and not smoke and time.monotonic() < hard_deadline\n        write_outputs(arguments.results_dir, metrics, correct, feasible, evidence)\n    except Exception as error:\n        try:\n            metrics['correct'] = 0\n            write_outputs(arguments.results_dir, metrics, False, False)\n        finally:\n            if PLANE == 'search':\n                if isinstance(error, FatalBrokerTransportFailure):\n                    record_failure({'component': 'broker', 'category': 'transport_failure',\n                                    'operation': error.operation})\n                name = bounded_failure_name(type(error).__name__.lower(), 'evaluator_exception')\n                print('evaluator_exception type='+name+' message=evaluation failed', file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print('evaluator_failure', file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    finally:\n        if client is not None:\n            client.close()\n    return 0\n\n\n{\n  \"repository\": \"https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results\",\n  \"revision\": \"6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383\",\n  \"source_row_count\": 126,\n  \"n_columns\": 135,\n  \"normalization\": \"NFKC; split/join whitespace; sorted JSON keys; integral numbers canonicalized; semantic task/version/scores excluding source IDs and timing\",\n  \"coverage_rule\": \"supported English main metric; one modal dataset revision/metric/split per task/subset with >=32 rows globally; one maximal-coverage model revision; rows >=12 cells; text-only modalities and exact main_score identity from official MTEB definitions at 5a83aafe4e7140d0606b96f59448c704f31dbf76; unsupported dynamic definitions excluded\",\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Heuristic family labels cannot certify undisclosed training ancestry.\",\n    \"Pinned snapshot lacks a LICENSE file; current official repository declares CC0-1.0; task.md attributes CC0-1.0 to data. No claim of historical license proof.\",\n    \"Underlying benchmark question documents are not fetched or used; examples here are real score result documents/rows.\",\n    \"Only observed-score support and queryable reservoir are evaluated; no generative LLM generalization.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocation\": \"string\"\n}\n[\n  \"aggregation\",\n  \"bootstrap\",\n  \"checkpoints\",\n  \"controls\",\n  \"episodes\",\n  \"expected_control_behavior\",\n  \"final_correct\",\n  \"max_candidate_rpc_calls\",\n  \"max_chunk_decoded_bytes\",\n  \"max_chunks\",\n  \"max_logical_transfer_bytes\",\n  \"observations_per_trajectory\",\n  \"operation_counts\",\n  \"reservoir\",\n  \"schema_version\",\n  \"search_correct\",\n  \"split\"\n]\n32:BASELINES = ['column_mean', 'copy_skill', 'random_low_rank', 'variance_low_rank', 'linear_ridge']\n149:        self.reader = threading.Thread(target=self._drain, name='worker-stderr-reader')\n465:                    target = destination / source.relative_to(self.program.parent)\n466:                    target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n467:                    shutil.copyfile(source, target)\n731:            or {row['family'] for row in rows} & set(manifest['peer_families'])):\n732:        raise RuntimeError('source identity, alias or outer-family overlap')\n756:            raise RuntimeError('insufficient queryable/target support')\n759:        targets = [rows[index] for index in episode['test']]\n760:        if not history or not targets or set(episode['history']) & set(episode['test']):\n762:        if {alias for row in history for alias in row['aliases']} & {alias for row in targets for alias in row['aliases']}:\n763:            raise RuntimeError('history/target alias overlap')\n765:        test_docs = {document['content_sha256'] for row in targets for document in row['documents']}\n766:        if history_docs & test_docs or {row['row_sha256'] for row in history} & {row['row_sha256'] for row in targets}:\n767:            raise RuntimeError('history/target normalized overlap')\n768:        if episode['case'] == 'B' and {row['family'] for row in history} & {row['family'] for row in targets}:\n769:            raise RuntimeError('family holdout overlap')\n858:        reservoir, targets = sorted(shuffled[:cut].tolist()), sorted(shuffled[cut:].tolist())\n859:        if not targets or len(reservoir) < 8:\n861:        output.append((reservoir, targets))\n874:    if name in ['random_low_rank', 'variance_low_rank']:\n879:    for row, (reservoir, target) in enumerate(partitions_for_rows):\n888:            elif name == 'copy_skill':\n890:            elif name == 'linear_ridge':\n900:            losses[row, checkpoint_index] = error_pair(predicted, tests[row], target)[0]\n944:        for trajectory, (reservoir, targets) in enumerate(partition):\n960:                    result['mae'][trajectory, checkpoint], result['mse'][trajectory, checkpoint] = error_pair(predicted, tests[trajectory], targets)\n{\n  \"mae_dimensions\": [\n    32,\n    4\n  ],\n  \"baseline_dimensions\": [\n    5,\n    32\n  ],\n  \"selection_first\": [\n    80,\n    131,\n    86,\n    120,\n    59,\n    34,\n    62,\n    5\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
