{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '375,415p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; tail -9 memory.md; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\npaper_data = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\nmethod_names = ['column_mean','copy_skill','random_low_rank','variance_low_rank','linear_ridge']\ndef mean(values):\n    return sum(values)/len(values)\nfor case_name in ['A','B','C','D']:\n    case_records = [episode['solution']['cases'][case_name] for episode in paper_data['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']]\n    candidate_by_budget = [mean([mean([row[checkpoint] for row in record['mae_by_row_checkpoint']]) for record in case_records]) for checkpoint in range(4)]\n    baseline_means = {method_name:mean([mean([mean(row) for row in record['baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint'][method_index]]) for record in case_records]) for method_index,method_name in enumerate(method_names)}\n    print(case_name, 'candidate_by_budget',candidate_by_budget, 'baseline_aggregate',baseline_means)\nreference_data=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nprint('reference structure',list(reference_data.keys()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '375,415p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; tail -9 memory.md; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\npaper_data = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\nmethod_names = ['column_mean','copy_skill','random_low_rank','variance_low_rank','linear_ridge']\ndef mean(values):\n    return sum(values)/len(values)\nfor case_name in ['A','B','C','D']:\n    case_records = [episode['solution']['cases'][case_name] for episode in paper_data['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']]\n    candidate_by_budget = [mean([mean([row[checkpoint] for row in record['mae_by_row_checkpoint']]) for record in case_records]) for checkpoint in range(4)]\n    baseline_means = {method_name:mean([mean([mean(row) for row in record['baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint'][method_index]]) for record in case_records]) for method_index,method_name in enumerate(method_names)}\n    print(case_name, 'candidate_by_budget',candidate_by_budget, 'baseline_aggregate',baseline_means)\nreference_data=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nprint('reference structure',list(reference_data.keys()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"        \"gate_reason\": str(args.gate_reason).strip(),\n        \"prior\": prior,\n        \"new\": paragraph,\n    }\n    # History append must succeed before the live file changes so a crash\n    # mid-write can never lose the prior version.\n    _append_jsonl(history_path, record)\n    _atomic_overwrite(conclusions_path, paragraph + \"\\n\")\n    return 0\n\n\ndef _run_append_event(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Execute the default event-append mode.\"\"\"\n    if not args.global_memory_md or not args.global_memory_jsonl:\n        print(\n            \"append_memory: --global-memory-md and --global-memory-jsonl are required \"\n            \"in event-append mode\",\n            file=sys.stderr,\n        )\n        return 1\n    event_file = Path(args.event_file) if isinstance(args.event_file, str) and args.event_file else None\n    event = _ensure_required_fields(\n        _load_event(event_json=args.event_json, event_file=event_file),\n    )\n\n    local_memory_path = Path(args.local_memory_md)\n    global_memory_md_path = Path(args.global_memory_md)\n    global_memory_jsonl_path = Path(args.global_memory_jsonl)\n\n    _append_text(local_memory_path, _markdown_entry(event), header=LOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS)\n    _append_text(global_memory_md_path, _markdown_entry(event), header=GLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER)\n    _append_jsonl(global_memory_jsonl_path, event)\n    return 0\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Run the command-line entry point.\"\"\"\n    args = parse_args()\n    if args.write_conclusions:\n        return _run_write_conclusions(args)\n    return _run_append_event(args)\n- evidence: reference_query_plan.json passes exact-key/type-category/unique-query checks and every query appears in reference_query_plan.md. Queries cover ALS cold-start prediction, weighted conditional medians, V-optimal design, incomplete covariance shrinkage, approved tinyBenchmarks/Observational Scaling Laws/Sloth titles, approved MTEB title, and budgeted rating elicitation. Final metrics and 126-by-135 MTEB dimensions were checked against local artifacts. Architectural shifts remain empty; no outer component ablations or support-gating success claimed. No reference retrieval, network search, experiment execution, or prohibited-stage output occurred.\n- next_action: Pass the nine-query plan to the later reference-retrieval stage with exact-title restrictions for approved starter works, no citation-chain expansion, and immediate stop-and-log on accidental prohibited-content encounters.\n- tags: stop_reason=reference_query_plan_ready, Rejected generic optimization/benchmarking/paper-writing queries because they do not explain the actual estimator or measured budget tradeoff; rejected broad task-paraphrase searches for prohibited-literature risk., Rejected architecture transitions, optional leaderboards, unvalidated component attribution, and generic causal cross-fitting citations for lack of grounded relevance.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:31:48.780935+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Selected a thesis-first sparse embedding-score prediction study over a mechanism-superiority claim or campaign diary; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Framing adds no new experimental method evidence.\n- evidence: Independent final evaluation is completed and qualified via final.qualification.status/outcome; downstream_study and edit-context/prior-paper inputs are absent. Final MAE=0.040807843083862115 versus five-baseline minimum 0.045249969215420516. Evaluator code uses fixed sealed targets, two held-out conditions, three seeds, and paired component bootstrap with baseline-bound minima. Selected source is ALS with cross-fitted local residual medians; no matched outer zero-correction ablation exists. ICLR style text width is 5.5 inches; venue requires 8-9 body pages. No scientific execution or network access performed.\n- next_action: Specify exact method groups, full-width overview and direct comparisons, evidence limitations, page allocation and substantive supplement; then validate strategy JSON only.\n\nA candidate_by_budget [0.042576364503879666, 0.039430870926997395, 0.036766678272902975, 0.034476748971933396] baseline_aggregate {'column_mean': 0.06436711309859706, 'copy_skill': 0.2386065727924508, 'random_low_rank': 0.04685719869486391, 'variance_low_rank': 0.044794737363260596, 'linear_ridge': 0.045116500007979975}\nB candidate_by_budget [0.04789031945165622, 0.0449861471961888, 0.04251144389350775, 0.03782417145383074] baseline_aggregate {'column_mean': 0.06410716020729763, 'copy_skill': 0.23561868685892118, 'random_low_rank': 0.049333975665207246, 'variance_low_rank': 0.047450341012489156, 'linear_ridge': 0.04538343842286106}\nC candidate_by_budget [0.0643